<aside class="cart-drawer" data-cart-drawer aria-hidden="true" aria-label="Shopping bag">
  <div class="cart-drawer__backdrop" data-cart-close></div>
  <div class="cart-drawer__panel" role="dialog" aria-modal="true">
    <div class="cart-drawer__head">
      <span class="h4">Your bag</span>
      <button class="icon-btn" data-cart-close aria-label="Close">{% render 'icon', name: 'close' %}</button>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      data-scroll-hint: theme.js fades the bottom edge and shows a thin bar
      while there is more below. Reported live on 6 November 2026 - a bag of
      five products looked like a bag of two on an iPhone, because iOS hides
      the scrollbar until a finger is already moving and nothing else said the
      list continued.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="cart-drawer__items" data-cart-items data-scroll-hint>
      {% if cart.item_count > 0 %}
        {%- comment -%}
          ONE PRODUCT, ONE ROW.

          Shopify splits a cart line whenever a discount reaches only some of
          its units, and the split is permanent: the free-gift discount covers
          exactly one unit (total_allocated_amount 595, read off the live cart
          on 6 November 2026), so five deodorants arrive as a line of 4 and a
          line of 1, both at full price, both correct and both confusing. The
          client reported it as a bug twice.

          The split cannot be prevented - it is Shopify's own arithmetic - so
          it is merged on the way out instead. The FIRST line of a variant
          renders the row, carrying the whole variant's quantity and price;
          the later ones are skipped. data-merge-keys passes the skipped keys
          to the stepper, which empties them before setting this one, so the
          cart really does collapse to a single line the moment the shopper
          touches it.

          GIFT LINES ARE NEVER MERGED. A gift is identified by the _free_gift
          property, not by its price or its collection, and it stays its own
          row with its own Remove.

          rendered_variants is a string because Liquid has no set. The pipes
          are the delimiter, so "|123|" cannot match inside "|4123|".

          The cart page runs the same block - sections/main-cart.liquid. Change
          one and change both, or the drawer and the page disagree about what
          the bag holds.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign rendered_variants = '' -%}
        {% for item in cart.items %}
          {%- assign is_gift = false -%}
          {%- if item.properties['_free_gift'] -%}{%- assign is_gift = true -%}{%- endif -%}

          {%- assign skip_line = false -%}
          {%- unless is_gift -%}
            {%- comment -%}
            The key is the variant AND its properties. A personalised towel for
            Ada and one for Ela are the same variant and two different orders:
            merging them hid one name, and the stepper then wrote the hidden
            line to zero. Fragments of one split line share their properties,
            so they still merge. url_encode keeps the pipes a true delimiter
            whatever a shopper types as a name.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- capture vkey -%}|{{ item.variant_id }}{%- for prop in item.properties -%};{{ prop.first | url_encode }}={{ prop.last | url_encode }}{%- endfor -%}|{%- endcapture -%}
            {%- if rendered_variants contains vkey -%}
              {%- assign skip_line = true -%}
            {%- else -%}
              {%- assign rendered_variants = rendered_variants | append: vkey -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endunless -%}

          {%- unless skip_line -%}
            {%- assign row_qty = item.quantity -%}
            {%- assign row_price = item.final_line_price -%}
            {%- assign merge_keys = '' -%}
            {%- unless is_gift -%}
              {%- assign row_qty = 0 -%}
              {%- assign row_price = 0 -%}
              {%- for other in cart.items -%}
                {%- unless other.properties['_free_gift'] -%}
                  {%- capture other_vkey -%}|{{ other.variant_id }}{%- for prop in other.properties -%};{{ prop.first | url_encode }}={{ prop.last | url_encode }}{%- endfor -%}|{%- endcapture -%}
                    {%- if other_vkey == vkey -%}
                    {%- assign row_qty = row_qty | plus: other.quantity -%}
                    {%- assign row_price = row_price | plus: other.final_line_price -%}
                    {%- unless other.key == item.key -%}
                      {%- assign merge_keys = merge_keys | append: other.key | append: ',' -%}
                    {%- endunless -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endunless -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endunless -%}

          <div class="cart-line{% if is_gift %} cart-line--gift{% endif %}" data-cart-line data-line-key="{{ item.key }}">
            <div class="cart-line__img"><img src="{{ item.image | image_url: width: 200 }}" alt="{{ item.product.title }}" width="200" height="200"></div>
            <div>
              <div class="cart-line__title">{{ item.product.title }}</div>
              {%- unless item.variant.title contains 'Default' -%}<div class="cart-line__variant">{{ item.variant.title }}</div>{%- endunless -%}
              {%- for prop in item.properties -%}
                {%- assign prop_prefix = prop.first | slice: 0 -%}
                {%- unless prop.last == blank or prop_prefix == '_' -%}
                  <div class="cart-line__prop">{{ prop.first }}: <strong>{{ prop.last }}</strong></div>
                {%- endunless -%}
              {%- endfor -%}

              {%- if is_gift -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  NO STEPPER ON A GIFT. The free-gift discount covers one unit,
                  so pressing + on this line put a second copy in the bag at
                  full price - which is exactly how a shopper ends up being
                  told their gift is being charged. One is the only quantity a
                  gift has, so the control that could change it is gone and
                  Remove is the only thing left to press.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <p class="cart-line__gift">{% if item.final_line_price > 0 %}Full price{% else %}Free gift{% endif %} &middot; 1</p>
              {%- else -%}
                {%- assign line_max = item.product.metafields.custom.max_per_order.value | default: 5 -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  The cap is the PRODUCT's, so it is measured against the
                  product's quantity across the cart rather than this row's -
                  a product can still hold two rows here when two variants of
                  it are in the bag.

                  Gift lines are excluded on purpose. A gift is not something
                  the shopper chose to buy and its quantity cannot be changed,
                  so counting it against a per-order cap only takes a paid
                  unit away from them. theme.js counts the same way: it sums
                  the steppers, and a gift line no longer has one.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- assign product_total = 0 -%}
                {%- for other in cart.items -%}
                  {%- unless other.properties['_free_gift'] -%}
                    {%- if other.product_id == item.product_id -%}
                      {%- assign product_total = product_total | plus: other.quantity -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endunless -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
                {%- comment -%}
  /cart/update.js takes any quantity with a 200 - four of a variant stocked at
  two, tested live on 6 November 2026 - and a merged row has to write through it.
  So a merged row carries what is left for it, after the variant's other lines
  including a gift, and theme.js holds the write to that. Blank means no limit.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign row_stock = '' -%}
{%- if merge_keys != blank and item.variant.inventory_management == 'shopify' and item.variant.inventory_policy == 'deny' -%}
  {%- assign row_stock = item.variant.inventory_quantity | plus: row_qty -%}
  {%- for other in cart.items -%}
    {%- if other.variant_id == item.variant_id -%}{%- assign row_stock = row_stock | minus: other.quantity -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- assign row_stock = row_stock | at_least: 0 -%}
{%- endif -%}
<div class="qty cart-drawer__qty" data-drawer-qty data-line-key="{{ item.key }}" data-merge-keys="{{ merge_keys }}" data-stock="{{ row_stock }}" data-product-id="{{ item.product_id }}" data-max="{{ line_max }}">
                  <button type="button" data-drawer-qty-dec aria-label="Decrease quantity">&minus;</button>
                  <input type="number" value="{{ row_qty }}" min="0" max="{{ line_max }}" inputmode="numeric" data-drawer-qty-input aria-label="Quantity for {{ item.product.title | escape }}">
                  <button type="button" data-drawer-qty-inc aria-label="Increase quantity">+</button>
                </div>
                {%- comment -%}
                  One element, two jobs. It states the standing per-order limit
                  when the line already sits at it, and the stepper writes into
                  it when a press of + cannot be honoured - a stock ceiling or
                  the cap - because this is the only place the shopper is
                  looking at that moment. Rendered even when it has nothing to
                  say so the stepper always has somewhere to write.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <p class="cart-line__limit" data-line-note data-line-key="{{ item.key }}" role="status"{% unless product_total >= line_max %} hidden{% endunless %}>
                  {%- if product_total >= line_max -%}
                    {%- if line_max <= 3 -%}Shipping weight limits this to {{ line_max }} per order.
                    {%- else -%}Limited to {{ line_max }} per order.{%- endif -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                </p>
              {%- endif -%}
              <a href="#" data-cart-remove data-line-key="{{ item.key }}" data-merge-keys="{{ merge_keys }}" class="cart-drawer__remove">Remove</a>
            </div>
            <div class="cart-line__price">{{ row_price | money }}</div>
          </div>
          {%- endunless -%}
        {% endfor %}
      {% else %}
        <div class="cart-empty" style="text-align: center; padding: var(--space-7) var(--space-4);">
          <p class="muted">Your bag is empty.</p>
          <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}" class="btn btn-outline mt-3">Shop bestsellers</a>
        </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    {% if cart.item_count > 0 %}
      <div class="cart-drawer__foot">
        <div class="cart-totals"><span>Subtotal</span><span>{{ cart.total_price | money }}</span></div>
        {%- comment -%}
          Shipping and gift progress used to be two separate blocks with two
          bars. They are one bar with two milestones now - see cart-gift.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {% render 'cart-gift' %}
        <a href="/checkout" class="btn btn-primary btn-block btn-lg">Checkout &middot; {{ cart.total_price | money }}</a>
        {%- comment -%}
          A text link rather than a second full-width button. On a phone this
          block was taking half the screen and leaving two rows for the
          products - reported 6 November 2026 - and a ghost button the same
          size as Checkout was the largest single piece of that.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <a href="{{ routes.cart_url }}" class="cart-drawer__viewbag">View bag</a>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Deliberately OUTSIDE the item_count guard above, and outside the panel.

    theme.js refreshes this drawer with drawer.innerHTML = newDrawer.innerHTML,
    and a <script> inserted through innerHTML never executes. So the gift
    picker's handler only ever runs on a real page load. While it lived inside
    cart-gift, a shopper who arrived with an empty cart never got it at all -
    the block had not rendered, so the tag was never in the document. They
    would add products, the drawer would refresh and show the chips, and
    clicking one did nothing until they reloaded the page. Rendering the assets
    unconditionally means the delegated listener is registered once at load and
    survives every later swap.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% render 'cart-gift-assets' %}
</aside>
